# SyncroMove: evaluation

All numbers below come from `docs/evaluation_results.json`, written by
`python scripts/evaluate.py` (run {{raw:generated_at}}, algorithm `{{raw:algorithm_version}}`, {{raw:runtime_seconds.total}} s
on a laptop-class CPU). **Nothing is trained or tuned.** The script only replays history and counts.

## Protocol

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| Data | `{{raw:dataset.file}}`: {{int:dataset.rows_raw}} rows → {{int:dataset.rows_after_dedup}} after dropping exact duplicates → {{int:dataset.rows_after_collapse}} after collapsing back-to-back repeats at the same venue; {{int:dataset.users}} users |
| Test window | The last {{pct:dataset.test_fraction}} of de-duplicated check-ins by time, from **{{raw:dataset.cutoff_utc}} UTC** |
| No peeking | City popularity is counted only from check-ins before the window. Each prediction uses only that user's earlier check-ins |
| Query | For every test check-in that has an earlier check-in: build the profile, score with the check-in's real time as the query time, record the rank of the place actually visited (miss if not a candidate) |
| Scored | **{{int:dataset.test_checkins}}** check-ins from {{int:full_extras.users_evaluated}} users, every one counted |

